# Runtime data (jobs.db, logs, exports, reports) — never bake into the image.
# This pattern is ROOT-ANCHORED: it excludes `backend/data/` only. Do NOT widen
# it to `**/data` — `src/data/uk_gazetteer/` is packaged code-data that the UK
# gate cannot run without, and shipping without it is issue #260 (four days of
# foreign jobs in a UK-only catalog, with every instrument green).
data/

# ...EXCEPT the data that is not runtime state but SHIPPED REFERENCE DATA.
#
# `.gitignore` deliberately un-ignores these same two directories, which is the
# whole reason they are committed. This file did not mirror that, and the
# Dockerfile is `COPY . .`, so the build threw away exactly the files someone had
# gone to the trouble of exempting — and nothing rebuilds them at deploy time.
# Railway volumes start empty, so no mount could supply them either.
#
# What that cost, silently and with no error:
#   uk_gazetteer/  — the ~52k UK place names rule #30 is built on. Without it
#                    `uk_gate._read()` returns an empty frozenset (it degrades
#                    rather than raising), so no job can match a UK place and the
#                    gate falls through to source-trust and ad-text evidence.
#   job_signals/   — the seniority / workplace / location term tables behind
#                    `signal_backed_lookup`, which fills 'unknown' enrichment at
#                    read time, and `detect_seniority`. `_load_terms` returns {}
#                    on a missing file, so those detectors quietly answer nothing.
#
# Both failure modes are invisible: empty data, no exception, no log line.
# `tests/test_shipped_data.py` now pins the two ignore files together.
# uk_gazetteer is NOT listed here any more, and its absence is deliberate:
# the data moved to `src/data/uk_gazetteer/`, and the `data/` rule above is
# ROOT-ANCHORED, so it never reached inside src/ in the first place. An
# exemption for a path nothing excludes is noise that reads like protection.
# What actually carries it into the image is
# `[tool.setuptools.package-data]` in backend/pyproject.toml plus
# `pip install .` — the wheel, not this file.
# NOTHING IS EXEMPTED HERE ANY MORE, and that is the fix, not a regression.
# job_signals/ MOVED to `src/data/job_signals/` on 2026-08-13, following the
# gazetteer. The `data/` rule above is ROOT-ANCHORED, so it never reached inside
# src/ — and, more importantly, an exemption here was never enough on its own:
# it put the files at /app/data, which only the API process can see (uvicorn
# inserts "." at sys.path[0]). The ARQ worker imports src from site-packages
# (arq/cli.py appends cwd) and found nothing. `[tool.setuptools.package-data]`
# in pyproject.toml is what carries them now — the wheel, not this file.

# Python caches
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache*/
# The glob matters: this repo carries .mypy_cache_core/, .mypy_cache_prof/ and
# .mypy_cache_routes/ (26.1 MB, untracked from git in 57625b6 but still on disk).
# A bare `.mypy_cache/` matches none of them, so a `railway up` from a developer
# machine shipped them into the image (backend/Dockerfile:13 is `COPY . .`).
*.egg-info/

# Virtual environments
.venv/
venv/
env/

# Tests (optional — kept out to slim the image; the test suite is offline only)
tests/

# Version control
.git/
.gitignore

# Editor / IDE artifacts
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo

# Local env overrides
.env
.env.*
